Here is the full **testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit** of `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs`.

---

## ① Summary Dashboard

```
┌──────────┬─────────────┬────────────────┐
│ Severity │ Smell Count │ Affected Tests │
├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┤
│ High     │ 3           │ 3              │
│ Medium   │ 2           │ 2              │
│ Low      │ 0           │ 0              │
├──────────┼─────────────┼────────────────┤
│ Total    │ 5           │ 5*             │
└──────────┴─────────────┴────────────────┘
* NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay carries two smells
```

**Integration-test calibration applied:** The class is annotated `[TestCategory("Integration")]`. Mystery Guest, Eager Test, and Sleepy Test severity are calibrated accordingly. Despite the integration marker, `Thread.Sleep` remains High because even integration tests should use async polling or event-based waits, not blind sleeps.

---

## ② Findings by Severity

### HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**Smell:** [testsmells.org — Unknown Test / Empty Test](https://testsmells.org)
**Test:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (line 113)
**Risk:** False confidence — this test passes even if every insert silently corrupts data, as long as no exception is thrown.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — no assertion
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

**Fix:** Assert the observable outcome:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

---

### HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**Smell:** [testsmells.org — Conditional Test Logic](https://testsmells.org)
**Test:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (line 95)
**Risk:** One branch is never exercised. Since a standard `User` is inserted, the `PremiumUser` branch never runs — the discount-rate assertion is dead code.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — if/else changes which assertion executes
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

**Fix:** Split into two tests with deterministic types:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed — one test per type
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsName()
{
    var user = new User("eve@example.com", "Eve");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasDiscountRate()
{
    var user = new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m);
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;

    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

---

### HIGH — Sleepy Test

**Smell:** [testsmells.org — Sleepy Test](https://testsmells.org)
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 82)
**Risk:** 3-second blind sleep slows the suite and is non-deterministic — if the notification takes 3.1 s the test flakes. Even in integration tests, sleep-based synchronization is unreliable.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — blind Thread.Sleep
Thread.Sleep(3000);
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Fix:** Use a polling helper or async event:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed — poll with timeout instead of blind sleep
[TestMethod]
public async Task NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay()
{
    var user = new User("dave@example.com", "Dave");
    _repository.Insert(user);

    var sent = await PollUntilAsync(
        () => _repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id),
        timeout: TimeSpan.FromSeconds(10),
        interval: TimeSpan.FromMilliseconds(200));

    Assert.IsTrue(sent, "Notification was not sent within the timeout.");
}
```

---

### MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**Smell:** [testsmells.org — Assertion Roulette](https://testsmells.org)
**Test:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (line 28)
**Risk:** Four assertions with no messages. When one fails in CI, the failure log shows `Assert.AreEqual failed` with no context about *which* property was wrong.

```csharp
// ❌ Current — 4 assertions, zero messages
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

**Fix:** Add a message to each assertion:

```csharp
// ✅ Fixed — each assertion explains what it checks
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "User should be retrievable after insert.");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should round-trip.");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should round-trip.");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Id should be auto-assigned by the database.");
```

---

### MEDIUM — Magic Number Test

**Smell:** [testsmells.org — Magic Number Test](https://testsmells.org)
**Test:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)
**Risk:** `3000` has no context — is it a contractual SLA, an arbitrary guess, or a measured p99?

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000); // ❌ What does 3000 mean?
```

**Fix:** Extract to a named constant:

```csharp
private static readonly TimeSpan NotificationGracePeriod = TimeSpan.FromSeconds(3);
// ...
await Task.Delay(NotificationGracePeriod); // ✅ Self-documenting
```

*Note:* `Assert.AreEqual(3, users.Count)` in `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` is **not** flagged — three items were inserted immediately above, making the value self-documenting.

---

## ③ Smells Scanned — No Findings (Clean)

The remaining **14 of 19** academic smells were scanned and are **clean**:

| Smell | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Mystery Guest | ✅ Clean | SQLite `:memory:` is an in-memory fake, not an external resource. Calibrated for integration scope. |
| Eager Test | ✅ Clean | No test calls 4+ distinct production methods. |
| Sensitive Equality | ✅ Clean | No `.ToString()`-based comparisons. |
| Exception Handling | ✅ Clean | No `try`/`catch` blocks in any test. |
| General Fixture | ✅ Clean | Both `_connection` and `_repository` are used by every test. |
| Ignored/Disabled Test | ✅ Clean | No `[Ignore]` attributes. |
| Duplicate Assert | ✅ Clean | No identical assertion pairs. |
| Lazy Test | ✅ Clean | Tests exercise distinct behaviors. |
| Constructor Initialization | ✅ Clean | Uses `[TestInitialize]` correctly. |
| Default Test | ✅ Clean | Class name is descriptive. |
| Redundant Print | ✅ Clean | No `Console.WriteLine` calls. |
| Redundant Assertion | ✅ Clean | No tautologies (`Assert.IsTrue(true)`). |
| Resource Optimism | ✅ Clean | In-memory DB avoids resource assumptions. |
| Empty Test | ✅ Clean | All tests have executable statements. |

**Well-designed tests worth noting:** `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase`, `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord`, and `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` are clean, focused, and properly structured.

---

## ④ Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Test | Impact | Effort |
|---|---|---|---|---|
